      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e what specifically makes this fail only on Lynx?\n\nThe failure shouldn\u0027t be specific to Lynx (although I only get to test on Lynx). Sorry for the confusion.\n\n\u003e long term really callers should deal with EXDEV being returned from rename() and do the correct thing themselves\n\nTo provide some background: I\u0027m from ARC (Android on Chrome) team. The motivation for this CL is that we need to port (or \"upstream\") all ARC-specific changes that exist only in the ARC branches into the main branch due to the Trunk Stable project (http://go/android-trunk-stable). This CL is for upstreaming http://ag/13353067.\n\nIn ARC, `/storage/emulated/0/Download` and the rest of `/storage/emulated` live in different device. This causes `ScopedStorageDeviceTest#testRenameDirectory` to fail only in ARC due to EXDEV when a non-empty directory is moved from `/storage/emulated/0/DCIM` to `/storage/emulated/0/Download` ([code](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:cts/hostsidetests/scopedstorage/device/src/android/scopedstorage/cts/device/ScopedStorageDeviceTest.java;l\u003d1861-1863;drc\u003da2d2cd70ec75c9ef2ea35f907d946915746e8c89)), and http://ag/13353067 was submitted to fix this.\n\nSo, an alternative to this CL would be to modify `ScopedStorageDeviceTest#testRenameDirectory` to handle the ARC-specific EXDEV on the test side. I\u0027m not sure which option is better.",
